n/id #uuid "561c8b40-300f-5972-9cb7-d1c7e137d94c" :question/math-academy-id "q-106756" :question/problem "Which of the following products is the LU factorization of a matrix $A?$\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]$\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that in the LU factorization of a matrix $A,$ we write $A=LU$ where the matrix $L$ is a unit lower triangular matrix (a lower triangular matrix that has only $1$'s on the main diagonal) and the matrix $U$ is an upper triangular matrix:\n\n$$\nA=\\overset{L}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{U}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each product in turn.\n\n- The first product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the left is not a unit lower triangular matrix, as its main diagonal contains a number not equal to $1.$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The second product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- The third product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106756/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2c1a562-1b3d-5180-9fef-e20ea916b17a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106756"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75116/selection/78529858181e56e516b48806c00986a04b52328e21aa6577062f3349937d3722" :answer/id #uuid "aed94dd4-e9fc-5fa2-82d1-bcead7840944" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II  and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75116/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "2179555b-e5be-5253-a034-f72262a95e85" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75116/selection/f8bc450b7f4fe2953896918c1f5c69e16edb279ae4186289918e142ef04a634f" :answer/id #uuid "f34205b5-7d1b-58eb-81b3-5ca44907c5bc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75116/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "4a94bb33-cead-5d93-b766-fef1bb914340" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75116/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "e12f20f8-e01a-5810-9222-23f9c6740052" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75116/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a6e46ab9-108a-591e-ab6f-d82f0a8875e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75116/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-75116/selection/78529858181e56e516b48806c00986a04b52328e21aa6577062f3349937d3722" "q-75116/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-75116/selection/f8bc450b7f4fe2953896918c1f5c69e16edb279ae4186289918e142ef04a634f" "q-75116/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-75116/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75116" :question/id #uuid "0df2a893-643b-575a-a7ea-beeb0878eb97" :question/math-academy-id "q-75116" :question/problem "Which of the following products is the LU factorization of a matrix $C?$\n\n- $C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\n- $C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\n- $C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that in the LU factorization of a matrix $C,$ we write $C=LU$ where the matrix $L$ is a unit lower triangular matrix (a lower triangular matrix that has only $1$'s on the main diagonal) and the matrix $U$ is an upper triangular matrix:\n\n$$\nC=\\overset{L}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{U}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each product in turn.\n\n- The first product is *not* in $LU$ form  because  the matrix on the left is not a unit lower triangular matrix, as its main diagonal contains a number not equal to $1.$\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The second product is *not* in $LU$ form. Although we have a product of an upper triangular matrix on the left and a unit lower triangular matrix on the right, the order of multiplication is not correct (instead, we need a unit lower triangular matrix on the left and an upper triangular matrix on the right).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The third product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix. \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-75116/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2c1a562-1b3d-5180-9fef-e20ea916b17a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75116"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75123/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "87280531-bbac-56ff-b1c6-2101d3d81d0e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75123/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "5112bbbd-5832-5bf9-bce6-11bc50588e06" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75123/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "ea6ac2ab-b8da-5e37-b874-2f692d2758d3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75123/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "b821af6a-6134-5ff9-9237-3970d0900a0c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75123/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "a0ad22ea-7408-5ec0-93ac-c2d6dfea1dc5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75123/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "89e59694-d8e4-5c45-af4d-cd6a323b3873" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75123/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-75123/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-75123/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-75123/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-75123/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-75123/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75123" :question/id #uuid "cf39dfe9-67f5-5e6d-9cc0-9139a83a257b" :question/math-academy-id "q-75123" :question/problem "Which of the following products is the LU factorization of a matrix $C?$\n\n- $C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\n- $C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\n- $C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that in the LU factorization of a matrix $C,$ we write $C=LU$ where the matrix $L$ is a unit lower triangular matrix (a lower triangular matrix that has only $1$'s on the main diagonal) and the matrix $U$ is an upper triangular matrix:\n\n$$\nC=\\overset{L}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{U}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each product in turn.\n\n- The first product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix. \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- The second product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the left is not a unit lower triangular matrix, as it has a non-zero entry above the main diagonal. \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The third product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the left is not a unit lower triangular matrix, as it has an entry not equal to $1$ on the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-75123/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2c1a562-1b3d-5180-9fef-e20ea916b17a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75123"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75117/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "18b5e184-d34f-54fa-88ae-c0c81bc02f31" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75117/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "84f6c03e-03bb-55c2-981d-bc0c46ac5a49" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75117/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "e0cea277-e795-5628-810b-154b8f8f03dd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75117/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "0f2cd858-ef76-53c5-88c7-0d73bb2dc5d4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75117/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "2b8c1e1b-38f4-5c0f-8b1b-6e01129f225f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75117/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fff4cd8a-ccdb-552a-9396-f0c67531ad2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75117/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-75117/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-75117/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-75117/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-75117/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-75117/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75117" :question/id #uuid "ad548fbf-72e6-5c5c-8b8c-7946f3fae039" :question/math-academy-id "q-75117" :question/problem "Which of the following products is the LU factorization of a matrix $A?$\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that in the LU factorization of a matrix $A,$ we write $A=LU$ where the matrix $L$ is a unit lower triangular matrix (a lower triangular matrix that has only $1$'s on the main diagonal) and the matrix $U$ is an upper triangular matrix:  \n\n$$\nA=\\overset{L}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{U}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each product in turn.\n\n- The first product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the left is not a unit lower triangular matrix, as it has an entry not equal to $1$  on the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The second product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the right is not an upper triangular matrix, as it has a non-zero entry below the diagonal. \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The third product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-75117/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2c1a562-1b3d-5180-9fef-e20ea916b17a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75117"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106751/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "e4cf3bcb-a448-5c8e-be86-51e491d37e3e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106751/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "864658f6-e9b1-5682-a994-b1b566adc814" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106751/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "456d8242-c3b8-5c4e-b356-e2b5bfd3a0de" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106751/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "b0b1980c-bb75-57a0-8541-483bc1e37d21" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106751/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "67409960-aebe-50ac-b4a4-7097a63d6b2c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106751/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c885e955-93bd-5f75-8eee-6a7f3152fde2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106751/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-106751/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-106751/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-106751/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-106751/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-106751/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106751" :question/id #uuid "7ac476d2-1a16-503d-a9ca-4392d9e5325c" :question/math-academy-id "q-106751" :question/problem "Which of the following products is the LU factorization of a matrix $A?$\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]$\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that in the LU factorization of a matrix $A,$ we write $A=LU$ where the matrix $L$ is a unit lower triangular matrix (a lower triangular matrix that has only $1$'s on the main diagonal) and the matrix $U$ is an upper triangular matrix:\n\n$$\nA=\\overset{L}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{U}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each product in turn.\n\n- The first product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- The second product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the left is not a unit lower triangular matrix, as its main diagonal contains a number not equal to $1.$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The third product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the right is not an upper triangular matrix, as it has a non-zero entry below the diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106751/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2c1a562-1b3d-5180-9fef-e20ea916b17a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106751"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106765/selection/5763f502e7862c7300798f2ed278f332eb678ae986a9aed59b215d3537006842" :answer/id #uuid "9c8dbc26-713e-54b4-b13f-1324d7b41cd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106765/selection/eaa39b3336b60a8707c77aa7ebffcb649539f9e1da48ae6fb0b3e2bd8e156958" :answer/id #uuid "efa6632f-d057-544f-839d-6882be353d56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106765/selection/9d409c41b1df4f52c174a12315f2ec16a37a97ea490ea81da2c6c5bccb086065" :answer/id #uuid "f5bbd2a9-bed0-575d-8cc3-0d6aadb877ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106765/selection/3691fd16acf6fbd3a61bbc1d619b3fdd1aaef53f19ba9f0a57ea993eee533ae9" :answer/id #uuid "8e587c53-0bc5-596a-9d98-65308425290f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106765/selection/83b0f59c64a4157d526937a73c0dec755f8afb56600bcf523ab04b591e8f5394" :answer/id #uuid "007cd6b9-5961-5cca-9e2f-b9a12752da6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106765/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "48d48022-7300-5aa5-90f6-d0a03764a0ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106765/selection/3691fd16acf6fbd3a61bbc1d619b3fdd1aaef53f19ba9f0a57ea993eee533ae9" :answer-field/choices ["q-106765/selection/5763f502e7862c7300798f2ed278f332eb678ae986a9aed59b215d3537006842" "q-106765/selection/eaa39b3336b60a8707c77aa7ebffcb649539f9e1da48ae6fb0b3e2bd8e156958" "q-106765/selection/9d409c41b1df4f52c174a12315f2ec16a37a97ea490ea81da2c6c5bccb086065" "q-106765/selection/3691fd16acf6fbd3a61bbc1d619b3fdd1aaef53f19ba9f0a57ea993eee533ae9" "q-106765/selection/83b0f59c64a4157d526937a73c0dec755f8afb56600bcf523ab04b591e8f5394"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106765" :question/id #uuid "5b8d761f-f823-50d6-82e7-47b259a96a25" :question/math-academy-id "q-106765" :question/problem "Given that \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 14 & -5\\end{aligned}]$ \nhas the LU decomposition $A=LU,$ then $L=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 14 & -5\\end{aligned}] & \\,{R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}\\,⟺\\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106765/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9279d979-74ba-5504-b98a-63692db3af72"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106765"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106762/selection/594f4371237f716a4e7b771cfac6a2ca8b8eb3c8dcb7752f2b3291728275476a" :answer/id #uuid "4db5ca9d-e1a1-593d-ab08-498091ef6757" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106762/selection/845beb42e162b04150b7b438e2c57c85fb9c5dc5bb6c7f2891f90687bf680708" :answer/id #uuid "c3c9641b-cc93-5f41-8ae4-8a4eaff592fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106762/selection/60d8696f019bd6901d4028773e8b64c56a3047a6bc6b4ed12b314cf6b1ae175a" :answer/id #uuid "ecebc37c-b4b0-5192-a77d-8d6fdff65b04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106762/selection/e0e0a3ac4fe95f021c8f8aece7092270d36ad30c356733db1e628dc4f0b1d434" :answer/id #uuid "1a53941a-5fd0-53dc-9ad8-c692e621ac8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106762/selection/6d8a7c7e73b503e82ee3fdeaeeda8131c0106d9ecb6a16ba218483b62acd0090" :answer/id #uuid "1ae59ec4-55d1-538c-b999-1c598ede39fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106762/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9958143f-c7e7-53e8-afc2-f454da6b186a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106762/selection/845beb42e162b04150b7b438e2c57c85fb9c5dc5bb6c7f2891f90687bf680708" :answer-field/choices ["q-106762/selection/594f4371237f716a4e7b771cfac6a2ca8b8eb3c8dcb7752f2b3291728275476a" "q-106762/selection/845beb42e162b04150b7b438e2c57c85fb9c5dc5bb6c7f2891f90687bf680708" "q-106762/selection/60d8696f019bd6901d4028773e8b64c56a3047a6bc6b4ed12b314cf6b1ae175a" "q-106762/selection/e0e0a3ac4fe95f021c8f8aece7092270d36ad30c356733db1e628dc4f0b1d434" "q-106762/selection/6d8a7c7e73b503e82ee3fdeaeeda8131c0106d9ecb6a16ba218483b62acd0090"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106762" :question/id #uuid "379569de-64d9-5eb2-98d5-cc05e5335c87" :question/math-academy-id "q-106762" :question/problem "Given that\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 15 & -4\\end{aligned}]$ \nhas the LU decomposition $A=LU$, then ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{22}=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 15 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1}\\,⟺\\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${l}_{21}=-5,{u}_{22}=6,$ and ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{12}=-30.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106762/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/i